{
  "name": "duplicate-vulns",
  "integration": "cyberint",
  "description": "REGRESSION LOCK. Every domain's FIRST alert used to be imported twice: build() seeded the list with `related_assets[domain] = [vuln]` when the domain was new and then fell through to an UNCONDITIONAL `related_assets[domain].append(vuln)`, so alert one landed twice and every later alert once. The seed is now an empty list and the append is the only place a finding is added.\n\nThe count is pinned with the 99-child cap rather than an equality assertion, because the harness can only assert a MINIMUM vulnerability count: 99 alerts all naming dup.example.com must yield exactly 99 findings, and the duplicated first alert makes it 100, which the `child_caps` invariant rejects. This scenario therefore fails for as long as the duplication exists.\n\nSkips namespaced_ids: cyberint ids are the domain with dots replaced by dashes and carry no tenant scope, a separate defect reported with the happy scenario.",
  "kwargs": {
    "url": "$BASE",
    "access_token": "fixture-cyberint-cookie"
  },
  "routes": [
    {
      "name": "alerts",
      "match": {"method": "POST", "path": "/alert/api/v1/alerts"},
